# PART 3 — PROGRAMME AND ADVERTISEMENT SHARING

Every published programme and every promotional campaign should be shareable through a proper URL.

This is important for WhatsApp, Facebook, Instagram DMs, LinkedIn, X and other platforms.

## 3.1 Programme sharing

Every publicly available programme should have a stable, canonical and shareable URL.

Use the existing programme route:

`/programs/:slug`

For example:

`https://jaystarblissstudios.com/programs/python-programming`

Use the actual programme slug generated or stored by the system. Do not invent URLs from titles when a valid slug already exists.

Add a visible Share action to programme detail pages.

The sharing interface should support:

- Native device sharing using the Web Share API where available.
- Copy Link as a fallback.
- A success notification after copying.
- An appropriate accessible share icon.

Sharing must work on desktop and mobile.

## 3.2 Social link previews

When someone shares a programme link, the preview should display the actual programme's:

- Title.
- Short description.
- Featured programme image.
- Canonical URL.
- Jaystarbliss Studios identity.

Populate the appropriate metadata:

- `og:title`
- `og:description`
- `og:image`
- `og:url`
- `og:type`
- `twitter:card`
- `twitter:title`
- `twitter:description`
- `twitter:image`
- Canonical URL.

The preview image must be the actual programme artwork, not the generic website favicon.

Where appropriate, add valid `Course` or `EducationalOccupationalProgram` structured data without inventing unsupported facts.

### Critical implementation requirement

The current website uses a client-rendered React/Vite application.

Changing document metadata with React after a page loads is not sufficient for many social-media crawlers. Some crawlers will read the initial HTML without executing the React application.

Therefore, implement a crawler-accessible metadata solution for dynamic programme links.

Investigate the existing Netlify architecture and implement the least disruptive reliable solution, such as:

- A Netlify Edge Function that resolves published programme data and returns the correct initial HTML metadata to social crawlers.
- A suitable prerendering solution.
- Another verified server-rendered metadata approach compatible with the current deployment.

Normal browser visitors must continue receiving the actual React application.

Do not return a fake static preview or expose private programme data to crawlers.

The current `MetaTagsContext.tsx` also contains a legacy `.name.ng` production URL. Reconcile canonical URL generation with the production domain already configured in `netlify.toml`. Use the configured production base URL consistently; do not generate legacy or mixed-domain share links.

Test dynamic metadata using real crawler-style requests that do not execute JavaScript.

## 3.3 Advertisement and campaign sharing

