## 4.3 School students must also be able to enrol independently

This requirement is particularly important.

A school student should not be restricted to the programmes already assigned to their school.

A student in a partner school may discover another published Jaystarbliss programme and decide to enrol independently.

For example:

A student is already learning through a school-provided Technology programme.

They visit Learning & Tracks, open Explore Programmes, find a separate Music programme, select it and submit a request.

That request is made by the student's authenticated portal account.

The new Music programme is treated as a **student-funded additional programme**, not as a new school subscription.

The school must not automatically receive the bill.

The student's existing school-funded programmes, institutional contract, school billing arrangements and assigned curriculum must remain untouched.

The student's additional programme must have its own:

- Enrolment request.
- Approval status.
- Approved fee.
- Billing responsibility.
- Payment history.
- Payment status.
- Renewal information.

The student should be able to manage the additional programme through their own portal.

Do not create a new parent account or convert the student into an individually registered student just because they are adding a self-funded programme.

Maintain the original school relationship and registration type.

