# PART 9 — PERSONAL PROGRAMME BILLING FOR INDIVIDUAL AND SCHOOL STUDENTS

This is one of the most important parts of the implementation.

**A school student who independently enrols in an additional programme must be billed as an individual payer for that specific programme. The school must not be charged for it.**

An individually enrolled student must also be able to manage their own programme fees.

A student may have more than one funding relationship at the same time.

For example:

- School-provided Mathematics: school-funded.
- School-provided Technology: school-funded.
- Independently selected Music programme: student-funded.

These must remain separate.

