- `nextDueDate`.
- `createdAt`.
- `approvedAt`.
- `updatedAt`.
- `approvedBy`.

You may choose a better schema after reviewing the existing system, but maintain the same clear separation of ownership, admission, billing and payment states.

### Security requirements

- A student may submit an application only for their own authenticated account.
- A school student may independently request an additional student-funded programme.
- A school student must not alter their `schoolId`, programme fee or billing responsibility through client-side writes.
- A student must not approve their own application.
- A student must not alter the administrator-approved fee.
- A student may access only their own self-funded programme fee records.
- A parent may request programmes only for verified linked children.
- Parents must not access unrelated family records.
- Only authorized administrators may approve applications and modify approved billing terms.
- Paystack reconciliation must use privileged server-side operations.
- No client-side writes may mark a transaction successful.
- Public programme reads must not expose private student or financial records.

Use Firestore rules that match the actual queries and access patterns.

Do not solve permission errors by broadly allowing public read/write access.

Add necessary Firestore indexes.

Review the security rules for existing legacy collection aliases before removing or consolidating anything.

